Subject: [EXPERIMENT] wifi: brcmfmac: rebuild transport after image restore

test_resume restores the host's message-buffer state from the frozen image,
but the running firmware has already processed the intervening thaw and image
I/O. Sending the D0 mailbox over those rewound rings produces invalid packet
IDs and eventually leaves the bus down.

Keep the normal resume and hibernation thaw paths stateful. On the distinct
restore transition, use the existing model-scoped, opt-in function 0 FLR path
to stop DMA and rebuild firmware, rings and packet IDs. Other systems retain
the existing hot-resume behavior.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2976,8 +2976,20 @@ cleanup:
+static int brcmf_pcie_pm_restore(struct device *dev)
+{
+	if (!brcmf_t2_recovery_flr)
+		return brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3(dev);
+
+	dev_info(dev,
+		 "t2wifi-restore: rebuilding transport after image restore\n");
+
+	return brcmf_pcie_reset(dev);
+}
+
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops brcmf_pciedrvr_pm = {
 	.suspend = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
 	.resume = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
 	.freeze = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
 	.thaw = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
 	.poweroff = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
-	.restore = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
+	.restore = brcmf_pcie_pm_restore,
 };
